    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Design a numerical experiment to test the hypothesis that the minimal network width $N_c(w)$ exhibits a phase transition (rigid vs. fat) as a function of constraint count $w$. We will generate synthetic constraint functions (analytic or algebraic) with known solution-space geometry, train small MLPs on $w$ points, and scan hidden widths to find the minimum $N_c(w)$ achieving zero violation (max error $\\le 10^{-3}$). The goal is to determine if $N_c(w)$ remains bounded (rigid) or diverges (fat) as $w$ increases, and whether this correlates with manifold dimensionality or NTK complexity. We will use multiple constraint families (low-rank linear, nonlinear manifold, high-curvature) to probe the \"if and only if\" claim about low-dimensional NTK representation."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "explore"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "For low-dimensional constraint manifolds (e.g., linear or low-rank nonlinear), $N_c(w)$ will remain small and sublinear in $w$ (rigid regime). For high-dimensional or ill-conditioned manifolds, $N_c(w)$ will grow superlinearly or fail to converge within scan limits (fat regime). The transition point will align with the Kolmogorov-Zurbenko complexity threshold."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "target_files"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "plan_id",
      "value": "plan_a9301557"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "status",
      "value": "completed"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "success",
      "value": true
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "objectives.score",
      "value": 0.0
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "script",
      "value": "import numpy as np\n\ndef family(kind, w, seed):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    if kind == 'rigid':\n        X = np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, w).reshape(-1, 1)\n        Xv = np.linspace(0.02, 0.98, 200).reshape(-1, 1)\n        coeffs = rng.standard_normal(3)\n        y = poly_basis(X, 3) @ coeffs\n        yv = poly_basis(Xv, 3) @ coeffs\n    elif kind == 'fat':\n        X = np.linspace(0.05, 0.95, w).reshape(-1, 1)\n        Xv = np.linspace(0.02, 0.98, 200).reshape(-1, 1)\n        coeffs = rng.standard_normal(10)\n        y = poly_basis(X, 10) @ coeffs\n        yv = poly_basis(Xv, 10) @ coeffs\n    else:\n        raise ValueError('kind must be rigid or fat')\n    scale = np.std(np.concatenate([y.flatten(), yv.flatten()]))\n    if scale > 1e-10:\n        y = y / scale\n        yv = yv / scale\n    return {'X': X, 'y': y, 'Xv': Xv, 'yv': yv}\n\ndef run(cfg):\n    seed = int(cfg.get('seed', 0))\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    w_vals = [3, 5, 10, 20]\n    h_vals = [4, 8, 16, 32]\n    N_c_rigid = []\n    N_c_fat = []\n    for w in w_vals:\n        N_c = None\n        for h in h_vals:\n            model = mlp_fit(family('rigid', w, seed)['X'], \n                            family('rigid', w, seed)['y'], \n                            h, seeds=3)\n            pred = mlp_predict(model, family('rigid', w, seed)['Xv'])\n            err = np.max(np.abs(pred - family('rigid', w, seed)['yv']))\n            if err <= 1e-3:\n                if N_c is None:\n                    N_c = h\n                break\n        N_c_rigid.append(N_c if N_c is not None else 999.0)\n        for h in h_vals:\n            model = mlp_fit(family('fat', w, seed)['X'], \n                            family('fat', w, seed)['y'], \n                            h, seeds=3)\n            pred = mlp_predict(model, family('fat', w, seed)['Xv'])\n            err = np.max(np.abs(pred - family('fat', w, seed)['yv']))\n            if err <= 1e-3:\n                if N_c is None:\n                    N_c = h\n                break\n        N_c_fat.append(N_c if N_c is not None else 999.0)\n    return {'success': True, 'summary': {'rigid_Nc': N_c_rigid, 'fat_Nc': N_c_fat},\n            'objectives': {'score': 0.0}}"
    },
